Z||000000||AusFiero||04-05-2001||11:36 AM||||Here are a couple of small pics taken by another Aussie friend on a Pontiac enthusiast jaunt to the USA. Got VIP treatment at Pontiac and shown around among many other cool things along the way. Was 50 people in all, I had to bail thanks to building my house (bummer).<BR>Anyway 3 89 GTs still exist and are just sitting there. Will endevour to borrow the original photos to get higher resolution versions to post.<BR>Also check out  <A HREF="http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page2.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pontiworld.com.au/newsletter/july2000/page2.html</A>  for more pictures of stuff inside the Pontiac development area.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/fieroforum.pip</A> <P><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||saleenfiero||04-05-2001||06:25 PM||||The fact that they sit outside in the elements is just sickening, well actually, most of those other cars can rot, but those 89's! Sacrelige!<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||11
